---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout>
    <main class="container mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 md:px-8 py-4 sm:py-6 md:py-8">
        <div class="mb-4 sm:mb-6">
            <a href="/home" class="inline-flex items-center px-2 py-2 bg-gray-200 hover:bg-[#00bbff40] text-white rounded-[50%] transition-colors duration-200 back-button cursor-none">
                <svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 448 512" class="h-5 w-5 sm:h-6 sm:w-6" fill="#000000">
                    <path d="M9.4 233.4c-12.5 12.5-12.5 32.8 0 45.3l160 160c12.5 12.5 32.8 12.5 45.3 0s12.5-32.8 0-45.3L109.2 288 416 288c17.7 0 32-14.3 32-32s-14.3-32-32-32l-306.7 0L214.6 118.6c12.5-12.5 12.5-32.8 0-45.3s-32.8-12.5-45.3 0l-160 160z"/>
                </svg>
            </a>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-4 sm:mt-6 md:mt-8 mb-8">
            <h2 class="flex justify-center text-center text-2xl sm:text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold text-gray-600 font-reenie px-4">
                Behind the Scenes & Random Thoughts
            </h2>	
        </div>

        <!-- Sticky Scroll Content -->
        <div class=" projectcontent relative flex h-[40rem] justify-center space-x-10 overflow-y-auto rounded-md p-6 bg-gray-50">
            <div class="relative flex items-start px-4">
                <div class="max-w-3xl">
                    <!-- Project Overview Section -->
                    <div class="my-16">
                        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-6">AthlezTech - Designing Smarter Cricket Training</h2>
                        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
                            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-4 text-sm">
                                <div>
                                    <span class="font-semibold text-gray-600">Role:</span>
                                    <span class="text-gray-800 ml-2">UX/UI Designer, Brand Designer</span>
                                </div>
                                <div>
                                    <span class="font-semibold text-gray-600">Timeline:</span>
                                    <span class="text-gray-800 ml-2">3 months</span>
                                </div>
                                <div>
                                    <span class="font-semibold text-gray-600">Team:</span>
                                    <span class="text-gray-800 ml-2">Product Engineer, Hardware Designer, UI/UX Designer</span>
                                </div>
                                <div>
                                    <span class="font-semibold text-gray-600">Goal:</span>
                                    <span class="text-gray-800 ml-2">Design a mobile app for cricket performance analytics</span>
                                </div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Challenge Section -->
                    <div class="my-16">
                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-6">Understanding the Challenge</h2>
                        <div class="space-y-6">
                            <!-- Context -->
                            <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-700 mb-3">Context</h3>
                                <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                                    AthlezTech is a sports-tech startup developing a smart wristband for athletes.
                                    The first product phase focused on cricket batsmen, capturing player movements through embedded sensors.
                                </p>
                            </div>

                            <!-- Problem -->
                            <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-700 mb-3">Problem</h3>
                                <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed mb-4">
                                    Traditional cricket coaching heavily relies on subjective feedback from coaches. 
                                    Many talented players remain unnoticed due to favoritism or lack of access to proper analytics tools.
                                </p>
                                
                                <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-700 mb-3">Our goal was to build an accessible app that:</h4>
                                <ol type="i" class="list-roman ml-6 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
                                    <li>Syncs seamlessly with the device</li>
                                    <li>Visualizes real-time performance stats</li>
                                    <li>Provides objective insights to improve technique</li>
                                </ol>
                            </div>

                            <!-- Constraints -->
                            <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-700 mb-3">Constraints</h3>
                                <ol class="list-decimal ml-6 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
                                    <li>Limited budget (needed to use minimal hardware components performing multiple tasks)</li>
                                    <li>App needed to be simple enough for grassroots-level players</li>
                                    <li>Integration with wearable sensor data requirements</li>
                                </ol>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Research & Discovery Section -->
                    <div class="my-16">
                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-6">Research & Discovery</h2>
                        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-700 mb-3">Market Research</h3>
                                <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                                    I explored similar sports analytics apps such as SmartCricket BatSense and Zepp Baseball to understand:
                                    Common metrics tracked (bat speed, impact time, swing angle), Visualization styles and
                                    Gaps in existing UX and accessibility
                                </p>
                        </div>
                        <br>
                        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-700 mb-3">Constraints</h3>
                                <ol class="list-decimal ml-6 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
                                    <li>Limited budget (needed to use minimal hardware components performing multiple tasks)</li>
                                    <li>App needed to be simple enough for grassroots-level players</li>
                                    <li>Integration with wearable sensor data requirements</li>
                                </ol>
                            </div>
                            <br>
                        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-700 mb-3">Key Findings</h3>
                                <ol class="list-decimal ml-6 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
                                    <li>Players desired visual representation of their stances and swings, not just numbers.</li>
                                    <li>Coaches wanted a simple way to compare players and sessions.</li>
                                    <li>Most apps lacked localized and budget-friendly solutions.</li>
                                </ol>
                            </div>
                            <br>
                        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-700 mb-3">Feature Prioritization</h3>
                                <p class="text-large font-bold text-gray-600 mb-4">To manage scope, I applied the MoSCoW framework:</p>
                                <ol class="list-decimal ml-6 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
                                    <li>Must have: Live stats (bat swing speed, angles, session graphs)</li>
                                    <li>Should have: Stance visualization (vectorized player animation)</li>
                                    <li>Could have: Personalized improvement suggestions</li>
                                    <li>Won’t have (for now): Social or community features
                                    </li>
                                </ol>
                            </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Solution Section -->
                    <div class="my-16">
                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-6">Designing the Experience </h2>
                        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-700 mb-3">Key App Flow:</h3>
                                <ol class="list-decimal ml-6 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
                                    <li>Mode Selection: Net Practice or Match Mode</li>
                                    <li>Real-Time Tracking: Device syncs with app to capture every shot</li>
                                    <li>Detailed Analytics: Each shot’s stats, swing speed, throughput & follow-through angles, hit/miss ratio</li>
                                    <li>Progress Visualization: Graphs comparing current and historical sessions</li>
                                    <li>Improvement Insights: Highlights repetitive mistakes for correction</li>
                                </ol>
                            </div> <br>
                        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
                            <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-700 mb-3">Unique Feature</h3>
                            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                               A vectorized player animation replicates the batsman’s real stance, bat swing, and angle allowing both player and coach to see posture issues in real time.
                            </p>
                        </div> <br>
                        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-700 mb-3">Design & Visual Identity</h3>
                                <p class="text-large font-bold text-gray-600 mb-4">Alongside UX design, I contributed to:</p>
                                <ol class="list-decimal ml-6 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
                                    <li>Logo & typography for brand identity</li>
                                    <li>Early waitlist website to attract initial users and build awareness before launch</li>
                                </ol>
                            </div>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Outcome section -->
                     <div class="my-16">
                        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-6">Outcome & Impact </h2>
                        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-700 mb-3">Impact</h3>
                                <ol class="list-decimal ml-6 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
                                    <li>The stance visualization feature was the most used and praised by testers.</li>
                                    <li>Coaches reported easier player feedback and performance tracking.</li>
                                    <li>Early prototypes gained attention from local cricket academies, validating product demand.</li>
                                </ol>
                            </div> <br>
                        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
                            <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-700 mb-3">Reflection</h3>
                            <p class="text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">
                               This project helped me merge UX design with hardware interaction, pushing me to think beyond screens — about how real-world motion translates to digital feedback.
                            </p>
                        </div> <br>
                        <div class="bg-white p-6 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-200">
                                <h3 class="font-bold text-lg text-gray-700 mb-3">If given more time, I’d:</h3>
                                <ol class="list-decimal ml-6 space-y-2 text-gray-600">
                                    <li>Improve onboarding for first-time device users</li>
                                    <li>Add a social comparison dashboard for team-based insights</li>
                                </ol>
                            </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="h-20"></div>
                </div>
            </div>
            
            <!-- Sticky Image -->
            <div class="addimage sticky top-20 hidden h-80 w-96 overflow-hidden rounded-xl shadow-lg lg:block">
                <img 
                    src="/athleztech.png" 
                    alt="Athleztech Project" 
                    class="w-full h-full object-cover"
                />
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>
</Layout>

<style>
    .font-reenie {
        font-family: 'Reenie Beanie', cursive;
    }

    .back-button {
        position: relative;
        overflow: hidden;
    }
    .projectcontent::-webkit-scrollbar {
        display: none;
    }
</style>